 "title": "Metabolic Pathways and Gene Regulation in Yeast and Other Organisms",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the metabolism of sulfur-containing compounds in yeast and other organisms. The yeast organism is central to this cluster, with various genes and proteins such as Pma1, V-ATPase, and Sch9 playing key roles in its metabolism. The metabolism of homocysteine, a key intermediate, is particularly prominent, with its conversion to cysteine, methionine, and hydrogen sulfide. The HSU1 gene has a pleiotropic role in sulfate utilization and is equivalent to the YLL058W gene. The MET17 gene catalyzes the conversion of homocysteine to cysteine and is deleted in the met17Δ strain. The cluster also includes various chemical compounds such as lysine, methionine, and hydrogen sulfide, which are involved in the metabolic pathways of yeast and other organisms.",
